-- The build tool as a package — the one whose descriptor the tool itself has to be able to read, and
-- as of v0.2 of the toolchain the one it can build.
--
-- **Three packages, no scopes, every one of them written out.** `root` is the library at `src/`, which
-- is what a consumer would get and what `//root` names; it says `at .` because its directory is the
-- repository's own and its name would have said otherwise. `launcher` is that library plus a platform
-- plus an entry point, and `test` is the suite at `test/src`. Nothing depends on either, so neither
-- one's platform layer reaches anybody — the isolation the old `artifact` and `test` scopes were
-- enforcing is the shape of the graph now (`docs/build-system.md`, "What this replaced, and why").
--
-- `launcher` is a package rather than a clause on the root, and it has to be: were `main
-- eliot.build.Launcher` declared in `root`, `test` would inherit it through `dep //root` alongside the
-- framework's runner, and the closure would hold two entry points.
--
-- `//stdlib` alone in the root package, because that is what `src` names: `eliot.collection.List`,
-- `eliot.file` and `eliot.system`. The `lang` layer arrives underneath it anyway — the eliot
-- repository's own descriptor says `package stdlib { dep //lang }` — and a dependency this package
-- does not import is not this package's to declare.
--
-- `v0.2` and not lower, everywhere: `src` performs `eliot.system.Process.registerExitCode`, which the
-- standard library grew at that tag, and the `plugin` clauses that say where the compiler binaries are
-- arrived at `v0.1`. A floor is a statement about what this code needs, and both halves of that are
-- true here for once — the sources and the toolchain that compiles them are the same requirement.
--
-- `test` declares the framework's own entry point, which under this design is the framework's to
-- declare about itself. It is written here because `eliot-test v0.0` is the only tag that exists and
-- it predates the `main` clause; a published tag is never replaced, so the line moves out of this file
-- the day a tag carrying it can be depended on.

package root {
  at .
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//stdlib v0.2
}

package launcher {
  dep //root
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//jvm v0.2
  main eliot.build.Launcher
}

package test {
  dep //root
  dep github.com/eliotlang/eliot-test v0.0
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//jvm v0.2
  main eliot.test.Runner
}
